.TH WEB 1 "September 2026" "web 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
web \- render a page or execute a finite browser plan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B web
get|read|text|html|links|snapshot URL [options]
.br
.B web
shot URL [out.png] [options]
.br
.B web
run [FILE|-] [--may-job JOB] [--attach ENDPOINT] [--keep | --tab ID]
.br
.B web
 auth URL [FILE] [--user-data-dir DIR] [--channel chrome] [--attach ENDPOINT] [--may-job JOB]
.br
.B web
setup|check|version|help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Web is an independent Go program using installed Chromium over CDP. It has no
model, task loop or shared runtime. Reads emit data to stdout; run emits one
JSON transcript. Diagnostics go to stderr. setup checks the installed browser;
check verifies embedded reduction fixtures offline.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --wait MODE
Read/goto readiness: domcontentloaded (default), load or networkidle.
.TP
.B --timeout MS
Read deadline, default 30000 milliseconds. Positive, at most 86400000.
.TP
.B --records-selector CSS
Snapshot records selected in the same evaluation as the page observation.
.TP
.B --profile FILE
Explicit cookies/origins storage-state JSON. Conflicts with --attach.
.TP
.B --attach ENDPOINT
Use the default context in a caller-owned browser. A port, HTTP(S) endpoint
or browser WebSocket URL. Never launches a fallback or closes that browser.
.TP
.B --keep
Run only: requires attach, retains its own tab only on success. Prints target ID.
.TP
.B --tab ID
Run only: requires attach, selects exactly this target and never closes it.
Conflicts with keep.
.TP
.B --may-job JOB
Use May's request JOB interface; exact action bytes go to its stdin. The
versioned machine verdict and exit status must agree before acting.
.TP
.B --stealth
Read/run/auth: inject pinned go-rod/stealth before new documents in the selected
tab. Off by default; no changes to unrelated tabs or approval gates. Existing
documents are not retroactively patched. No guaranteed bot-check bypass.
.TP
.B --user-data-dir DIR
Read/run/auth: launch with an explicitly selected persistent native browser
profile using Rod's NewUserMode argument preset. Conflicts with attach and JSON
profile. Web closes its launched process but retains the directory, even on
failure. Existing Chrome/Web locks are refused. Use attach for a running browser.
Chrome's default personal data directory is refused; remote debugging requires
a non-default directory in Chrome 136+. No credentials are copied to it.
.TP
.B --profile-directory NAME
Select a profile inside the native data directory (default Default). Requires
user-data-dir. A directory name, not a path.
.SH PLANS
A JSON array or object with steps. goto, click, type [CSS,text], select
[CSS,value], wait (CSS or milliseconds), read, html, shot and submit are
supported. Steps have optional timeout, may and irreversible fields. html's
out field writes complete markup to a file. Inline markup above 200000
characters fails. Password input is refused. See README.md for step shapes.
.PP
Every click, submit and irreversible:true step calls may request JOB with --may-job (or the legacy Clerk job variables),
otherwise asks y/N on /dev/tty. Plans cannot disable this. Attached/native auth
exports require approval before connecting or launching. Fresh auth waits for manual login
and Enter; EOF does not export JSON. Native auth may omit FILE and keeps browser
state in its data directory regardless of Enter/EOF. A prior valid login can be
reused; a new MFA challenge remains manual. Profiles are written atomically with mode 0600.
.SH OUTPUT
Snapshot version 1: requested_url, url, title, text, links and records. Each
link has label and url; each record has text and links. Snapshot output,
plan input and profile input are limited to 8 MiB. No partial snapshot stdout.
Run transcript: ok, ms and steps, with zero-based i, ok and operation result.
The first failure halts execution. A parked run restarts from the beginning.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
WEB_BROWSER selects Chromium. WEB_ATTACH_TIMEOUT bounds CDP connection
(default 10000 milliseconds). WEB_STATE selects audit JSONL; default is
XDG_STATE_HOME/web/web.jsonl or ~/.local/state/web/web.jsonl.
CLERK_WORKER, JOB_ID and CLERK_WROOT together select the May job gate.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 complete; 1 operation/browser failure; 2 invalid input; 3 declined;
64 unknown command; 75 parked; 77 no approver.
.SH FILES
Profiles contain cookies and localStorage from open origins. Closed origins,
IndexedDB, sessionStorage and passwords are not exported. Partitioned cookies
are refused on export/replay; use attach for those sessions. Browser profiles,
audit logs, screenshots and HTML output belong in caller-selected writable
locations, outside the installed source library.
.SH SEE ALSO
README.md, DESIGN.md
